endobj

339 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 89 0 R/T(Unfortunately, the 2018-19 season was really one to forget with The Ambers finishing in their lowest ever position of 8th and with poor showings in the Cup competitions. Colliver departed the club in the Autumn and, despite their best efforts, the interim management team of Steve Istead and Jon Froggatt were unable to lift the general malaise that had set in around the club.)/E(Unfortunately, the 2018-19 season was really one to forget with The Ambers finishing in their lowest ever position of 8th and with poor showings in the Cup competitions. Colliver departed the club in the Autumn and, despite their best efforts, the interim management team of Steve Istead and Jon Froggatt were unable to lift the general malaise that had set in around the club.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

340 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 89 0 R/T(At the end of the campaign, the decision was made for the club to continue on a much-reduced budget and to return to Olivers Mount. Russ Eagle was invited back to the club as Manager alongside Aiden Spowage, and to strengthen ties with the Junior Sporting Club, the new Management Board sought and gained approval from the NCEL to change the clubs name to Handsworth FC.)/E(At the end of the campaign, the decision was made for the club to continue on a much-reduced budget and to return to Olivers Mount. Russ Eagle was invited back to the club as Manager alongside Aiden Spowage, and to strengthen ties with the Junior Sporting Club, the new Management Board sought and gained approval from the NCEL to change the clubs name to Handsworth FC.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

341 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 89 0 R/T(The 2019-2020 and 2020-2021 campaigns saw the club suffer some highs and lows as was to be expected with such a young and changing squad, and after a hit and miss start to the 2021-22 season, The Ambers parted company with Eagle in October, with Aiden Spowage and Jason Dodsworth named as Joint Managers, with Louis Axcell strengthening the management team later.)/E(The 2019-2020 and 2020-2021 campaigns saw the club suffer some highs and lows as was to be expected with such a young and changing squad, and after a hit and miss start to the 2021-22 season, The Ambers parted company with Eagle in October, with Aiden Spowage and Jason Dodsworth named as Joint Managers, with Louis Axcell strengthening the management team later.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

342 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 89 0 R/T(An excellent run to the 3rd Qualifying Round of the FA Cup underpinned a highly respectable 8th placed finish, but despite the efforts of everyone involved, we were unable to build on this and a disappointing 2022-2023 campaign saw The Ambers finish in their lowest ever position of 16 th , leading to the inevitable departure of the management team.)/E(An excellent run to the 3rd Qualifying Round of the FA Cup underpinned a highly respectable 8th placed finish, but despite the efforts of everyone involved, we were unable to build on this and a disappointing 2022-2023 campaign saw The Ambers finish in their lowest ever position of 16 th , leading to the inevitable departure of the management team.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

343 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 89 0 R/T(Ambers\220 legend Jon Froggatt was handed the reins alongside Mark Ward ahead of the 2023-2024 season, and an excellent start saw The Ambers within touching distance of top spot, before a desperate run of form through the Winter saw the team drop alarmingly before a late resurgence claimed an improved 13th placed finish. Improvement continued the following season, with The Ambers securing an excellent 7th placed finish after an enjoyable, if sometimes frustrating season, a position The Ambers matched with a better points tally last season when they were still in the hunt for a play off spot until the penultimate game of the season.)/E(Ambers\220 legend Jon Froggatt was handed the reins alongside Mark Ward ahead of the 2023-2024 season, and an excellent start saw The Ambers within touching distance of top spot, before a desperate run of form through the Winter saw the team drop alarmingly before a late resurgence claimed an improved 13th placed finish. Improvement continued the following season, with The Ambers securing an excellent 7th placed finish after an enjoyable, if sometimes frustrating season, a position The Ambers matched with a better points tally last season when they were still in the hunt for a play off spot until the penultimate game of the season.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

344 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 89 0 R/T(With one of the lowest playing budgets in the division, The Ambers continue to punch above their and will be looking to push on even further this time around.)/E(With one of the lowest playing budgets in the division, The Ambers continue to punch above their and will be looking to push on even further this time around.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

