901 0 obj
<</Title(Simon Helsop)/Dest[18 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 897 0 R/Next 903 0 R>>
endobj

902 0 obj
<</Title(An excellent run to the 3rd Qualifying Round of the FA Cup underpinned a highly respectable 8th placed finish, but despite the efforts of everyone involved, we were unable to build on this and a disappointing 2022-2023 campaign saw The Ambers finish in their lowest ever position of 16 th , leading to the inevitable departure of the management team.)/Dest[29 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 904 0 R/Next 898 0 R>>
endobj

903 0 obj
<</Title(First Team Manager)/Dest[18 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 901 0 R/Next 905 0 R>>
endobj

904 0 obj
<</Title(The 2019-2020 and 2020-2021 campaigns saw the club suffer some highs and lows as was to be expected with such a young and changing squad, and after a hit and miss start to the 2021-22 season, The Ambers parted company with Eagle in October, with Aiden Spowage and Jason Dodsworth named as Joint Managers, with Louis Axcell strengthening the management team later.)/Dest[29 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 906 0 R/Next 902 0 R>>
endobj

905 0 obj
<</Title(Programme Ramble)/Dest[19 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 903 0 R/First 907 0 R/Last 908 0 R/Count -4/Next 909 0 R>>
endobj

906 0 obj
<</Title(At the end of the campaign, the decision was made for the club to continue on a much-reduced budget and to return to Olivers Mount. Russ Eagle was invited back to the club as Manager alongside Aiden Spowage, and to strengthen ties with the Junior Sporting Club, the new Management Board sought and gained approval from the NCEL to change the clubs name to Handsworth FC.)/Dest[29 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 910 0 R/Next 904 0 R>>
endobj

907 0 obj
<</Title(This weekend sees the return of the FA Cup with the 3rd Qualifying round games being played - Barton Town are representing the NCEFL when they entertain National North side Chorley - other Step 5 clubs still involved in the competition include SE Dons from the Southern Counties East League Premier Division - Trafford FC from the North West Counties League Premier - Tadley Calleva who compete in the Cherry Red Records Combined Counties Football League -)/Dest[19 0 R/Fit]/Parent 905 0 R/Next 911 0 R>>
endobj

908 0 obj
<</Title(It will be interesting how the league looks at the end of the month with a lot of games to be played in the next few weeks.)/Dest[19 0 R/Fit]/Parent 905 0 R/Prev 912 0 R>>
endobj

909 0 obj
<</Title(Pikes Team Stats)/Dest[20 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 905 0 R/Next 913 0 R>>
endobj

910 0 obj
<</Title(Unfortunately, the 2018-19 season was really one to forget with The Ambers finishing in their lowest ever position of 8th and with poor showings in the Cup competitions. Colliver departed the club in the Autumn and, despite their best efforts, the interim management team of Steve Istead and Jon Froggatt were unable to lift the general malaise that had set in around the club.)/Dest[29 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 914 0 R/Next 906 0 R>>
endobj

911 0 obj
<</Title(On paper Barton look to have the most difficult task when they play Chorley - Of the other teams -Trafford play Atherton Colleries from the NPL West Division - South East Dons travel to Southern League Division 1 South \(Step 4\) side Weymouth FC - although Weymouth have suffered successive relegations they are currently sitting at the top of their league - Tadley Calleve entertain Isthmian Premier Division \(Step 3\) side Dartford FC - looking at the season\220s results to date Trafford FC would seem to have best opportunity to progress, but as we all know about football results!!!)/Dest[19 0 R/Fit]/Parent 905 0 R/Prev 907 0 R/Next 912 0 R>>
endobj

912 0 obj
<</Title(Back to the NCEFL and Barton Town who beat us on Tuesday are now up to 5th place in the league and with games in hand over the teams above them - having reached the play offs last season they would have been one of the pre-season favourites to be challenging - but looking at top half of the league currently you probably wouldn\220t have predicted the it as it sits at the moment, with two of the top seven - Bottesford Town 2nd at present and Horbury Town 7th - flirting with relegation right to the end last season.)/Dest[19 0 R/Fit]/Parent 905 0 R/Prev 911 0 R/Next 908 0 R>>
endobj

